<Base title="A gift without expectations" description="Offering something thoughtful while leaving room for the person receiving it."><article class="prose"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / A gift without expectations</nav><p class="eyebrow">Bloom Library · Friends & family</p><h1>A gift without expectations</h1><p class="smallnote">New editorial draft · I Will Bloom · 17 November 2026</p><p>When someone you love is going through cancer, choosing a gift can feel surprisingly difficult. You may want to show care without asking them to reassure you or feel a particular way.</p><h2>Keep the message simple</h2><p>A note such as “Thinking of you. There is no need to reply” can leave space for whatever kind of day they are having.</p><h2>Let the gift belong to them</h2><p>If you give a journal, there is no need to ask to read it or check whether they have started. They may use it now, later, occasionally or in a way you did not expect.</p><p>You can offer practical help too: a specific errand, a meal or a lift, with an easy way to say no.</p><p><a href="/bloom-library/">← Back to the Bloom Library</a></p></article></Base>